# Z9X v6.2 power-off fix (install as /system/etc/init/z9x_poweroff.rc;
# script /system/etc/xgimi/z9x_poweroff.sh 0755 root:root).
# UNVERIFIED on the device: power-off tests T1-T4 must run with the user present.
#
# Root cause (research/v62/poweroff): the vendor watchdog driver wdt-mt5896.ko starts the PM-domain
# hardware watchdog at probe (30 s, kernel self-ping every 500 ms; counter/control registers at
# 0x1c020190..0x198, the always-on PM block) and its .shutdown hook stops it only when the watchdog
# core marks it WDOG_ACTIVE, i.e. only if userspace opened /dev/watchdog0. Nothing opens it on our
# GSI, so after 'reboot: Power down' the watchdog keeps counting and resets the chip
# (live: wdt_reset_chk = pm51-wdt-reset, /sys/mtk_pm wakeup_reason id = 0 after the auto power-on).
#
# Fix: only for a real power-off (sys.powerctl=shutdown*), open /dev/watchdog0, write the magic 'V'
# and close it (driver supports WDIOF_MAGICCLOSE, nowayout=0) -> watchdog core -> mtktv_wdt_stop.
# Reboot is NOT touched (the reboot path resets the chip through this same watchdog).
# Kill switch: persist.z9x.poweroff.wdtstop=0.
# 'exec' blocks init (shutdown_done waits behind it) and init sets no time limit, so the script
# only stops the watchdog synchronously; its diagnostics run in a detached background job
# (bounded by toybox 'timeout', 3 s) and the exec returns at once.
# It never stops/starts services.
on shutdown
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/etc/xgimi/z9x_poweroff.sh
